framework PurposeBusPluginV1Package:
  requires problem and decision
  requires premise and evidence
  warns pending

domain PurposeBus:
  description "Local-first coordination queue and Skill-only Codex Plugin"

problem P1:
  |
    What exact local package, compatibility contract, and behavioral evidence
    satisfy T_V1_PLUGIN_PACKAGE without changing active profiles, broadening the
    accepted surface, or publishing the Plugin?

premise PR1:
  |
    The owner accepted the immutable RC candidate and explicitly instructed the
    next PERT task to proceed. T_V1_PLUGIN_PACKAGE requires an exact Plugin 1.0
    package, compatible core range, manifest and Skill validation, repo
    marketplace metadata, supported-surface copy, sandbox and approval behavior,
    credential absence, fresh-session behavior, end-to-end request response, and
    disable or uninstall fallback.

premise PR2:
  |
    The same task excludes installation outside the accepted test scope and does
    not authorize workspace or public-directory publication, commit, push,
    release, deployment, an MCP component, or a changed remote surface claim.

premise PR3:
  |
    The accepted RC contract is historical candidate evidence. Moving the live
    Plugin source to the downstream 1.0 package must preserve the RC version and
    hashes as predecessor provenance instead of rewriting the accepted RC.

evidence EV1:
  |
    Current PERT digest 76bcec4141dea5068ed5965e4bd1c6855d238a6df546a6bec568400471b64a90
    reports V0_9_RC_ACCEPTED accepted with no blocking criterion and recommends
    only T_V1_PLUGIN_PACKAGE.

evidence EV2:
  |
    Local HEAD and an independently read GitHub feature/local-mvp ref both equal
    2a2b3a68c8f44a4107268e4fd51949106a37d486. Existing uncommitted beta and RC
    work remains in the same worktree and must be preserved.

evidence EV3:
  |
    The current source Plugin is Skill-only at version
    0.2.0+codex.20260904090953, requires exactly purposebus 0.2.0a1 at runtime,
    consumes purposebus.*.v2 and purposebus.error.v1, and has no MCP, app, hook,
    embedded credential, or direct database component.

evidence EV4:
  |
    The repo marketplace purposebus-local already resolves
    ./plugins/purposebus with AVAILABLE installation, ON_INSTALL authentication,
    and Productivity category. The Plugin and marketplace are currently visible
    from the configured local source, but the active installed Plugin remains the
    accepted 0.2 candidate.

evidence EV5:
  |
    Current official OpenAI Plugin documentation requires plugin.json, supports
    skills at the Plugin root, treats local marketplaces as distinct from public
    publication, and calls for complete Skill-only Plugin testing after local
    installation in a new conversation using direct, indirect, follow-up,
    negative, and unsupported or boundary prompts.

evidence EV6:
  |
    The installed Codex CLI supports marketplace add, Plugin add, list, and
    remove, but exposes no Plugin disable subcommand. Therefore an uninstall and
    raw CLI fallback is the directly supported local fallback check.

premise IN1:
  |
    Inference: only purposebus 0.2.0a1 has current end-to-end evidence for this
    Plugin contract. Declaring compatibility with future 0.2 or 1.0 core versions
    would be speculative, so the initial 1.0 Plugin contract should use the exact
    version specifier ==0.2.0a1 plus the v2 success, v1 error, and state-schema 1
    requirements. A later tested core candidate can revise the range.

premise ALT1:
  |
    Alternative: add the optional read-only MCP package to Plugin 1.0. This is
    rejected because the accepted post-trial surface is Skill-only and no new
    measured requirement justifies the lifecycle and authority expansion.

premise ALT2:
  |
    Alternative: install or update the active user Plugin profile. This is
    rejected because the task accepts an isolated test scope and active-profile
    mutation is a separate state boundary.

premise ALT3:
  |
    Alternative: use static package tests as a substitute for fresh-session
    behavior. This is rejected because it omits a material completion condition.

pending PD1:
  |
    Whether a fresh isolated Codex home can authenticate and load the candidate
    while using the existing auth object read-only is not yet observed. If it
    cannot, retain that as a blocker rather than replacing the behavioral test.

pending PD2:
  |
    Windows/Desktop GUI pickup and public submission review are outside the
    accepted local test scope and remain unverified.

decision D1 based_on P1, PR1, PR2, PR3, EV1, EV2, EV3, EV4, EV5, EV6, IN1, ALT1, ALT2, ALT3, PD1, PD2:
  |
    Start T_V1_PLUGIN_PACKAGE in the current worktree. Change the Plugin base
    version to 1.0.0 and use the plugin-creator cachebuster helper for one exact
    development candidate. Keep the Plugin Skill-only and freeze a machine
    contract with core specifier ==0.2.0a1, required CLI and response schemas,
    supported surfaces, absent components, authority limits, predecessor RC
    digests, critical file hashes, and the required five-class evaluation matrix.
    Update tests so the immutable RC remains historical provenance rather than a
    false live-Plugin invariant. Add a deterministic Plugin archive and verifier
    that validates the manifest, Skill, marketplace, package contents, secret
    absence, isolated install and cache readback, uninstall, and independent CLI
    fallback. Use only a temporary HOME, CODEX_HOME, state root, marketplace,
    and working directory for fresh Codex sessions; reference the existing auth
    object read-only without copying or printing it. Run direct, indirect,
    follow-up, negative, and cross-host boundary evaluations plus an isolated
    request-response workflow. If any material behavioral check is unavailable,
    stop with the task incomplete. Otherwise emit exact local evidence and finish
    T_V1_PLUGIN_PACKAGE. Do not change the active Plugin profile or marketplace,
    add MCP or apps, commit, push, publish, release, deploy, or start downstream
    release preparation.

query Q1:
  .document.steps[].statement | select(.role == "decision" and len(.based_on) > 0)
